      "logo": "https://garnerandtow.com/cdn/shop/files/GT_logo_primary_pos_100x.png?v=1740692443"
    },
    "publisher": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "Garner and Tow",
      "url": "https://garnerandtow.com",
      "logo": "https://garnerandtow.com/cdn/shop/files/GT_logo_primary_pos_100x.png?v=1740692443"
    },
    "articleBody": "When we started Garner and Tow, the goal was simple: build bags that could keep up with how people actually move through the world. Not just on a bike—but beyond it. Bags that didn't ask you to choose between function and form, or between riding and living. Over time, we noticed something. A lot of people weren't heading out on multi-day rides or weekend trips—they were commuting. Riding to work. Meeting friends after. Stopping at the grocery store on the way home. Their rides were shorter, but more frequent. More integrated into daily life. And while our original designs could absolutely handle that, we realized something important: daily riders deserve gear that's purpose-built for them. That's where The Everyday Line comes in.",
    "url": "https://garnerandtow.com/blogs/press/why-we-made-the-everyday-line"
